\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Okay so batch fourteen came back from the manufacturer and the pH stability data looked off. I went back to the supplier and it turns out they quietly changed the preservative blend without notifying us \'97 they sent a revised spec sheet three months ago but it got buried. The new preservative system is more acidic than the previous one. The finished product pH dropped by about 0.4 units which sounds small but it's enough to push us out of the optimal range for our emollient blend. The batch isn't unsafe but the texture is different in a way that I think customers will notice. We're holding it. I need to write about this because I think it illustrates something important \'97 the assumption that a 'same formula' reorder is actually the same formula. It often isn't. Suppliers change things. If you're not checking the CoA against a baseline every batch, you won't catch it until the customer does.}